   "reasoning_summary": "C10H12N2 has DoU 6, consistent with an indole. The 13C spectrum shows 8 sp2 carbons (111.8-139.1) and 2 sp3 CH2 carbons (42.4 CH2N, 25.4 ArCH2), matching tryptamine. In 1H, the four aromatic signals (7.71, 7.57, 7.32, 7.23) account for the 5 indole CH, with H2 and H6 overlapping at 7.32. Two CH2 signals appear at 3.33 and 3.18. Indole NH and NH2 are exchanged in D2O, so 9 non-exchangeable H are assigned. Shifts are slightly downfield, as expected for the protonated ammonium form in D2O. The absence of an upfield H3/C3 (~6.3/100 ppm) disfavours the 2-substituted isomer. The absence of an N-CH2 near 4.3 ppm rules out N1-alkylation."
